mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|sb|s|mb|3S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North had 4@S call. One good rule is to always bid 4 over limit raise with a singleton. Further, your hand has 15 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at|. Even if you discount the @DJ you have 10 HCP, 2 length points to start with (ignoring DJ), one extra point for 6th spade after fit, and 2 points for singleton.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 5 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With 15 Bergen declarer points you have enough to bid game. If I have only 10 might be close but you do have the @DJ. So I North has a clear 4@S bid not to mention very possible 10 card fit. No worries, since I have obvious 4♠ bid.|
PG| ***** 6 ***** |


mb|4C|mb|4S|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
